WHY THESE NUMBERS
=================

position (1024, 84.232421875, 1024)
    x/z = exact map centre. Map is 2048 x 2048.
    Also the centre of your PlayableArea, which is 356 x 356 at (846, 846),
    so it spans 846..1202 on both axes.
    y is copied verbatim from your existing edbm0149 prop, which already sits at
    map centre -- so that IS the terrain height there, already measured.
    Note: prop positions are absolute world elevation. RunMapSetup does NOT snap
    props to terrain (mapUtils.lua:94-100). Only alloy markers get snapped
    (mapUtils.lua:130-136). So y must be correct going in.

rotation = identity
    Prop holes are forced to rotation 0 at propTemplateLoader.lua:191 regardless.

scale = 1.0  <-- THE ONE THAT WILL BITE YOU
    Your existing centre prop (edbm0149) uses scale 50.0. If you copy that habit
    here, and instance scale DOES propagate to the hole, a 40-unit hole becomes
    2000 units -- larger than the entire 2048 map. It would read as either
    "nothing happened" or "the terrain broke", and you would not know which.
    Keep scale at 1.0 for the first run so you are measuring holeSize directly.
    Whether instance scale affects hole size is UNVERIFIED -- this test answers it.


BEFORE YOU LAUNCH
=================

Back up the .sanmap. You already have `Pandemonium Isthmus.sanmap.bak` from
2026-08-13; make a fresh one.

Reason, from your own project notes:

    "A BAD blueprintPath ABORTS THE REST OF MAP LOAD (confirmed in-game 2026-08).
     Props that DO resolve still render, but everything parsed after props --
     alloy/resource markers especially -- silently never spawns."

mapUtils.lua:107 calls Engine.Error() on an unreadable blueprint, which kills
RunMapSetup before the alloy block at :113.

So: if the .santp is not where the blueprintPath says it is, ALL 282 OF YOUR
ALLOYS DISAPPEAR, and the symptom points at markers, not at props.


PASS / FAIL, IN ORDER
=====================

1. Do your alloys still spawn?
       NO  -> the path is wrong. Nothing else below matters. Fix the path first.
       YES -> the .santp resolved and parsed. That alone is the main risk cleared.

2. Zoom the camera in close to map centre.
       PropRenderDistance is hardcoded to 80 (propTemplateLoader.lua:4).
       The hole only renders within 80 world units. On a 2048 map that is TIGHT.
       Do not conclude failure from a wide shot.

3. Is there a hole?
       YES -> holes work on props. The whole shatter feature is now unblocked
              and everything after this is placement and triggering.
       NO, but alloys spawned -> the template loaded but the hole did not render.
              Most likely causes, in order:
                a) still outside the 80-unit render distance
                b) holeSize semantics differ from what shipped structures imply
                   (try 6.0 to match ugs1511's circle hole exactly)
                c) y is wrong -- the hole may need to be at or just under terrain
                d) holes genuinely need a mesh present to render against; if so,
                   add a `visuals.lods` block borrowed from CrystCluster_B1


NEXT TEST AFTER IT WORKS
========================

Duplicate the entry with scale 2.0 instead of 1.0, at a different position.
If the second hole is twice the size, instance scale drives hole size -- which
means one prefab covers every hole size you will ever want, and random scale is
free. If it is identical, you need a ladder of fixed-size prefabs instead.

That single comparison decides the whole random-scale design.
